### Register a donor
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "donor1",
  "email": "donor1@test.com",
  "password": "TestPass123",
  "role": "donor"
}

### Register a receiver
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "receiver1",
  "email": "receiver1@test.com",
  "password": "TestPass123",
  "role": "receiver"
}

### Login as donor — copy the "access" token from the response
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "donor1",
  "password": "TestPass123"
}

### Login as receiver — copy the "access" token from the response
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "receiver1",
  "password": "TestPass123"
}

### Create donor profile (paste donor's access token below)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/donors/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer 

{
  "blood_group": "O+",
  "weight": 65,
  "age": 28
}

### Create receiver profile (paste receiver's access token below)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/receivers/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer 

{
  "hospital_name": "City Hospital",
  "contact_number": "9999999999"
}

### Create a blood request (as receiver)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/requests/blood-requests/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer 

{
  "blood_group_needed": "O+",
  "units_needed": 2
}

### List receiver's own requests (as receiver) — note the id of the request you just created
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/requests/blood-requests/
Authorization: Bearer 

### Get matching donors for that request (replace 1 with the actual request id)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/requests/blood-requests/1/matches/
Authorization: Bearer 